From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blissfulgit <blissfulgit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci: do not abort init when the controller rejects
 the default link policy

Some controllers, such as the Unisoc UWE5621/UWE5622 Wi-Fi + BT combo used
on many Amlogic TV boxes, answer HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY with
"Invalid HCI Command Parameters" (0x12). hci_sync then fails the whole
controller initialization and the adapter can never be brought up:

  Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x080f failed: -22
  Can't init device hci0: Invalid argument (22)

The controller is otherwise fully functional (it resets fine and reports a
valid BD_ADDR), so log the failure and keep going instead of making the
device permanently unusable.
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c
@@ -4334,6 +4334,7 @@ static int hci_setup_link_policy_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
 	struct hci_cp_write_def_link_policy cp;
 	u16 link_policy = 0;
+	int err;
 
 	if (!(hdev->commands[5] & 0x10))
 		return 0;
@@ -4353,8 +4354,13 @@ static int hci_setup_link_policy_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 
 	cp.policy = cpu_to_le16(link_policy);
 
-	return __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
-				     sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+	err = __hci_cmd_sync_status(hdev, HCI_OP_WRITE_DEF_LINK_POLICY,
+				    sizeof(cp), &cp, HCI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+	if (err)
+		bt_dev_warn(hdev, "failed to set default link policy (%d)", err);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int hci_read_page_scan_activity_sync(struct hci_dev *hdev)
